# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin panel — production environment
#
# Copy to /var/www/codeboujida/admin/.env on the server.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: Vite bakes these values into the JavaScript AT BUILD TIME.
# Editing this file changes nothing until you run `npm run build` again. There
# is no runtime configuration for a static site.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the panel sends its API requests.
#
# Leave it EMPTY (or delete the line): the panel then uses the relative path
# "/api", which resolves against whatever domain it was loaded from. That is
# correct for this deployment — panel and API share the origin codeboujida.com
# — and it means no CORS, and no rebuild if the domain ever changes.
#
# Set an absolute URL (https://api.example.com) ONLY if the API moves to a
# different hostname. In that case also fill CORS_ORIGINS in the API's .env,
# or the browser will block every request.
VITE_API_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT an environment variable: the panel is served from /admin, and that path
# is set in admin/vite.config.ts as `base: "/admin/"`. It also drives the
# router's basename. If you ever move the panel to a different path, change it
# there and in nginx/codeboujida.conf together, then rebuild.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
